codex
The fresh LLVM and Haskell definitions both built successfully. The loop invariant claim independently closes with exit 0 and `#Top`; the entry claim is still running when isolated from the loop claim, which is useful evidence about whether the claimed “independent” target actually depends on the circularity being present in the same proof run.
